# Project context (always)

Before architectural, deploy, env, or naming decisions, read and follow:

1. `@README.md` — monorepo map, local URLs, entry commands
2. `@docs/LOCAL.md` — `pnpm tpl` / start / stop / bootstrap / Docker local profile
3. `@docs/DEPLOY.md` — `pnpm remote`, hosts, compose envs
4. `@docs/ENV.md` — secrets and env layout under `env/`
5. `@docs/NAMING.md` — `I*` / `E*` / `T*` contracts conventions

When editing a package, also check its package README if present (`server/`, `client/`, `contracts/`).

## Monorepo layout

```txt
template/
  contracts/   Shared Zod schemas, types (I*/E*/T*), helpers
  server/      NestJS API + TypeORM migrations (nest mode: serve separately built SPA)
  client/      React Router v7 (Vite SPA in dev; deploy: nginx | ssr | nest | cdn)
  website/     Astro + React SSG (Docker locally + deploy; optional CDN)
  mcp/         MCP server (NestJS, HTTP + stdio)
  cli/         pnpm commands
  docker/      compose.yml + environments.json (server/client/mcp/website)
  deploy/      hosts.json (SSH hosts only)
  env/         Runtime secrets (gitignored). Local `env/*.env`; remote `env/<host>/*.env`
  scripts/     Deploy + docker-env loader
  docs/
```

## Commands (do not invent alternatives)

- Prefer `pnpm tpl` (menu) or `pnpm tpl start` / `pnpm remote`
- Do **not** use `pnpm setup`, `pnpm restart`, `pnpm pkg`, or `pnpm deploy` (reserved by pnpm/npm)
- Use `pnpm bootstrap`, `pnpm reload`, `pnpm add-pkg`, and `pnpm remote` instead

